@startuml video-pages-flow
title Fluxo do módulo Video Pages — API Orfanato NIB

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #37474F

actor "Admin" as Client
participant "VideosPageController" as Controller
participant "Create/Update/Delete\nVideosPageService" as Service
participant "VideoPageMediaService" as Media
participant "MediaStorageService\n(UploadBatch)" as Storage
database "VideosPageRepository\n(TypeORM)" as Repo
participant "S3" as S3

== Atualizar (PATCH /video-pages/:id) ==
Client -> Controller : multipart: videosPageData + arquivos
Controller -> Controller : JwtAuthGuard + AdminRoleGuard\nFeatureFlagGuard (page_management)\nvalidação do DTO (400)
Controller -> Service : execute(id, dto, arquivos)
Service -> Repo : findById (404 se não existe)
Service -> Repo : runInTransaction
activate Repo
Repo -> Repo : lockPage (FOR UPDATE)\nfindMedia (já dentro da transação)
Service -> Repo : removeMedia (linhas que saíram)
Service -> Media : materialize(cada vídeo)
Media -> Storage : uploadAll (arquivo novo)
Storage -> S3 : putObject (chave única)
Service -> Repo : saveMedia / savePage
Repo --> Service : commit
deactivate Repo
alt commit confirmado
  Service -> Storage : batch.commit()
  Service -> Storage : deleteAfterCommit(objetos antigos)
  Storage -> S3 : deleteKey (falha -> media_cleanup_queue)
else falha em qualquer passo
  Service -> Storage : batch.discard() (novos saem do bucket)
  note right : antigos intactos e referenciados\nlog só com a causa, sem stack
end

== Criar / Apagar ==
note over Service, Repo
  Criar: página + rota + mídia numa transação; objetos novos só ficam se ela confirmar.
  Apagar: linhas + página + rota numa transação; objetos saem do bucket depois do commit.
end note
@enduml
